# sing_all.lic
=begin
      author: Fizzlestiks
        name: sing_all
        game: gemstone
        tags: bard, loresing, loresong, recall, unlock
    requires: loresing.lic
     version: 1.1.1
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Runs ;loresing all <item> on everything in a container until RECALL says each item's
  loresong is unlocked.

  Usage:
    ;sing_all mantle           a container you're wearing or holding
    ;sing_all linen.mantle     adjective.noun, like the game

  First it kills song-manager and STOPs every song, so no renewal comes due while the
  loresinging is using the mana. song-manager stays off afterwards (Fizzlestiks-prep starts
  it again, or ;song-manager).

  Then, for each item in the container:
    - RECALL it. Already unlocked? Its stats print and it goes back, no singing.
    - ;loresing all <noun>, killed as soon as a verse fails.
    - From there it carries on at the verse that failed, with two couplets that have no
      keyword in them (loresing.lic's own "magic" one and another), taking turns. A song
      with no keyword sings the verse after the last one that worked, and a failure doesn't
      move the place, so nothing is sung twice. Singing the same thing twice running only
      "resonates with what you previously learned", which is why they alternate.
    - RECALL again once all four verses are in (or the song has come to its end). The stats
      mean it's unlocked. "You must reveal the entire loresong" starts ;loresing all over.
      Not in between: whether RECALL forgets the verses learned so far isn't on record.
    - Back in the container, and on to the next. After max_verses verses it gives up on that
      item and says so in the summary.

  The item is sung to from the right hand, because LORESING goes by the right hand: on 11/08
  with the mantle in the right hand every verse "failed to resonate" with the mantle. A
  container in the right hand is swapped to the left, and anything else in the right hand is
  put away and brought back at the end, when the container goes back to the right. playsongs
  is stopped (the drum takes both hands).

  1.1.0: carries on at the failed verse instead of starting ;loresing all over.
  1.1.1: a container taken from the right hand goes back to the right hand at the end.

  Game text this relies on, all from Fizzlestiks' logs unless noted:
    failed verse  "As you sing, you feel that the X has more to share, but your song simply
                   wasn't powerful enough to glean more."  (no roundtime)
    wrong noun    "As you sing, you feel a faint stirring in your X that fades, as if your
                   song had somehow failed to resonate with it properly."
    no mana       "Your song is weak, and without sufficient power to affect the X."
                  (gswiki Loresinging; not in the logs. Harmless, but the verse is wasted.)
    not a failure "Your music surrounds the X, but it simply resonates with what you
                   previously learned." / "You feel that you have reached the end of the
                   X's song."  (no harm done; the end means start over or it's unlocked)
    verse worked  "As you sing, you feel a faint resonating vibration from the X in your
                   hand..." and a "Roundtime: 7 sec."
    still locked  "You must reveal the entire loresong of the X before you can unlock it."
    unlocked      "As you recall your song, ..." / "As you recall Vonaq's song, ..." and at the
                   end "It has a permanently unlocked loresong by you."
                  ("temporarily unlocked loresong by a bard for 17 days" isn't enough: those
                   are sung to. Only seen on other characters' items so far.)
    STOP SINGING  "But you are not singing any spellsongs." / "You allow the lingering
                   effects of your songs to fade."  (STOP SING just gets "Stop what?")
=end

module SingAll
  VERSION = '1.1.1'

  # ---- the knobs (methods, so an edit takes effect on the next run)
  # The most verses to sing to one item, and the most times to start ;loresing all on it.
  # 10/27-11/19 a verse worked about two times in three (121 of 183 sung).
  def self.max_verses
    60
  end

  def self.max_passes
    8
  end

  # Two couplets with no keyword (value, weight, purpose, skill, enhance, spell, ability),
  # rhymed by spelling. The first is loresing.lic's magic verse.
  def self.plain_songs
    ['it will be helpful for me to know,;What magic within will you now show?',
     'that I hold in my hand,;Sing to me the finest song in the land']
  end

  # Don't sing a verse with less mana than this, and once it's that low (or the game says the
  # song has no power) rest until half. What a verse costs isn't on record; the two long
  # sessions (11/08, 11/16) work out to very roughly 2-4 mana each.
  def self.mana_floor
    20
  end

  def self.mana_resume
    [maxmana.to_i / 2, mana_floor].max
  end

  # ---- game text (see the header)
  WEAK       = /your song simply wasn't powerful enough to glean more/
  NO_POWER   = /^Your song is weak, and without sufficient power/
  WRONG_NOUN = /failed to resonate with it properly/
  UNLOCKED   = /^Its loresong has been permanently unlocked by you/
  VERSE_OK    = /^As you sing, you feel a faint resonating vibration from the /
  PREVIOUSLY  = /simply resonates with what you previously learned/
  END_OF_SONG = /^You feel that you have reached the end of the .+ song/
  NOTHING_NEW = /^You learn nothing new about/ # gswiki; not in the logs
  VERSE_DONE  = Regexp.union(WEAK, NO_POWER, WRONG_NOUN, PREVIOUSLY, NOTHING_NEW, /^Roundtime: \d+ sec/)
  # which of loresing.lic's four verses the game just echoed
  SUNG = {
    value: /What might be your own value/, purpose: /your purpose is what I would most like/,
    plain: /What magic within will you now show/, ability: /What special ability to you hold inside/
  }

  STILL_LOCKED = /^You must reveal the entire loresong/
  RECALLED     = /^As you recall (?<who>.+?) song, you feel a faint resonating vibration/
  RECALL_END   = /^It has a .*unlocked loresong by/
  TEMPORARY    = /^It has a temporarily unlocked loresong/
  NOT_HELD     = /^You must be holding .+ before you can unlock its loresong/
  RECALL_DONE  = Regexp.union(STILL_LOCKED, RECALL_END, NOT_HELD, /^Recall what|^I could not find|^What were you referring to/)

  STOP_DONE        = /^You stop singing|^But you are not singing|^You allow the lingering effects|^You are not singing|^Stop what/
  SONG_STATUS_DONE = /Your current renewal cost is \d+ mana\.|You are not singing any songs\./
  SONG_LINE        = /^\s+\((10\d\d)\) /

  CLOSED    = /^(?:That|The .+) is closed/
  LOOK_DONE = Regexp.union(/^Total items|^There is nothing in|^In the .+? you see|^I could not find|^What were you referring to/, CLOSED)
  GET_DONE  = /^You (?:remove|get|grab|pull|take|pick up|retrieve|already have)|^Get what|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|^You need a free hand|^You can't/
  PUT_DONE  = /^You (?:put|place|slip|tuck|add|drop)|^I could not find|^What were you referring to|won't fit|^That is closed|too (?:full|heavy|large)/
  SWAP_DONE = /^You swap|^You have nothing to swap/

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- small stuff
  def self.msg(text)
    respond "[sing_all] #{text}"
  end

  def self.bold(text)
    _respond "<pushBold/>[sing_all] #{text}<popBold/>"
  end

  def self.wait_for(seconds)
    end_time = Time.now + seconds
    until yield
      return false if Time.now > end_time
      sleep 0.2
    end
    true
  end

  # put, not fput (fput can take an unrelated line for the reply; see fizzpure). Reads until
  # `done`, or, once a line matching `settle` has been seen, until a second goes by quietly.
  def self.collect(action, done, timeout: 5, settle: nil)
    lines = []
    Script.current.clear
    put action
    end_time = Time.now + timeout
    last_line = Time.now
    loop do
      line = get?
      if line
        lines << line
        last_line = Time.now
        if line =~ /^(?:\.\.\.w|W)ait ([0-9]+) sec/
          sleep [Regexp.last_match(1).to_i - 0.5, 0.3].max
          put action
          end_time = Time.now + timeout
          next
        end
        break if line =~ done
      else
        break if settle && Time.now - last_line > 1.0 && lines.any? { |l| l =~ settle }
        sleep 0.1
      end
      break if Time.now > end_time
    end
    lines
  end

  def self.right_id
    GameObj.right_hand.id&.to_s
  end

  def self.left_id
    GameObj.left_hand.id&.to_s
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the container
  # "linen.mantle", "linen mantle", "my mantle", "mantle": the last word is the noun and every
  # other word starts a word of the name (same as orb_check / fizzpure)
  def self.matches?(obj, name)
    words = name.to_s.strip.sub(/\Amy\s+/i, '').split(/[\s.]+/)
    return false if words.empty? || obj.nil? || obj.id.nil?

    obj.noun.to_s.casecmp?(words.last) && words[0..-2].all? { |word| obj.full_name.to_s =~ /\b#{Regexp.escape(word)}/i }
  end

  # hands first, then worn
  def self.find_container(name)
    [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand, *Array(GameObj.inv)].find { |obj| matches?(obj, name) }
  end

  # a fresh LOOK IN, so the IDs are live. Opens it if it's closed.
  def self.look_in(container)
    waitrt?
    lines = collect("look in ##{container.id}", LOOK_DONE)
    if lines.any? { |line| line =~ CLOSED }
      fput "open ##{container.id}"
      collect("look in ##{container.id}", LOOK_DONE)
    end
    sleep 0.3
    Array(container.contents)
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- songs and hands
  def self.stop_script(name)
    return false unless Script.running?(name)

    Script.kill(name)
    wait_for(10) { !Script.running?(name) }
    true
  end

  def self.song_status
    text = collect('song status', SONG_STATUS_DONE, timeout: 4).join("\n")
    text.lines.map { |line| line[SONG_LINE, 1] }.compact.uniq
  end

  # song-manager first, or it sings them again
  def self.quiet_songs
    # a fizzpure_songs wait still pending would start song-manager again mid-run
    $fizzpure_songs_token = $fizzpure_songs_token.to_i + 1
    killed = stop_script('song-manager')
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    collect('stop singing', STOP_DONE, timeout: 3)
    song_status.each { |num|
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      collect("stop #{num}", STOP_DONE, timeout: 3)
    }
    left = song_status
    msg "#{killed ? 'Killed song-manager and stopped' : 'Stopped'} your songs." if left.empty?
    bold "Still singing #{left.join(', ')}, so its renewal can still come due." unless left.empty?
  end

  # right hand free for the items; the container, if it's held, in the left
  def self.free_right_hand
    if right_id && right_id == @container.id.to_s
      collect('swap', SWAP_DONE, timeout: 3)
      @swapped = wait_for(2) { left_id == @container.id.to_s }
    end
    return true if right_id.nil?

    empty_right_hand
    @emptied_right = true
    wait_for(3) { right_id.nil? }
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- moving items
  def self.hold(item)
    waitrt?
    collect("get ##{item.id}", GET_DONE, timeout: 4)
    wait_for(2) { [right_id, left_id].include?(item.id.to_s) }
    collect('swap', SWAP_DONE, timeout: 3) if left_id == item.id.to_s
    wait_for(2) { right_id == item.id.to_s }
  end

  # whatever's in the right hand goes back in the container
  def self.put_back
    2.times do
      return true if right_id.nil?

      waitrt?
      collect("put ##{right_id} in ##{@container.id}", PUT_DONE, timeout: 4)
      return true if wait_for(2) { right_id.nil? }
    end
    false
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- RECALL
  # :unlocked (for good), :locked, :not_held or :unknown. A bard's RECALL is also what unlocks
  # it once every verse is known; it has no roundtime and costs nothing.
  def self.recall(item)
    waitrt?
    lines = collect("recall ##{item.id}", RECALL_DONE, settle: RECALLED)
    text = lines.join("\n")
    if (who = text[RECALLED, :who])
      @owner = who == 'your' ? 'by you' : "by #{who.sub(/'s\z/, '')}"
      return text =~ TEMPORARY ? :locked : :unlocked
    end
    return :locked if text =~ STILL_LOCKED
    return :not_held if text =~ NOT_HELD

    msg "Didn't recognize the reply to RECALL. The game said:"
    lines.last(4).each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
    :unknown
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- loresinging
  def self.rest_for_mana(force = false)
    return if checkmana >= mana_floor && !force
    return if checkmana >= mana_resume

    msg "Resting until #{mana_resume} mana (you have #{checkmana})."
    sleep 2 until checkmana >= mana_resume || dead?
  end

  # loresing.lic speaks bard at the start and common at the end; killed early it leaves him
  # in Guildspeak, which is where the next verse wants him. finish/cleanup put it right.
  def self.kill_loresing
    @guildspeak = true if stop_script('loresing')
  end

  def self.speak(language)
    return if @guildspeak == (language == 'bard')

    fput "speak #{language}"
    @guildspeak = (language == 'bard')
  end

  # the verse after the last one that worked, for a song with no keyword
  def self.learned(kind)
    verse = { value: 1, purpose: 2, ability: 4 }[kind] || @place + 1
    @known |= [verse] if verse <= 4
    @place = [verse, 4].min
  end

  def self.all_known?
    (@known & [1, 2, 3, 4]).size == 4
  end

  # One run of ;loresing all. Returns :weak, :no_power or :wrong_noun if it was killed for
  # that, :unlocked if the game said so, :complete if that was the last verse needed, :done if
  # it sang all the way through.
  def self.loresing_pass(item)
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    Script.current.clear
    @guildspeak = false # loresing.lic sees to the language itself, unless it's killed
    unless Script.start('loresing', "all #{item.noun}")
      @stop_reason = "couldn't start loresing.lic"
      return :no_script
    end

    end_time = Time.now + 120
    exited_at = nil
    kind = nil
    loop do
      line = get?
      result =
        case line
        when WEAK       then :weak
        when NO_POWER   then :no_power
        when WRONG_NOUN then :wrong_noun
        when UNLOCKED   then :unlocked
        when VERSE_OK   then :ok
        end
      kind = SUNG.key(SUNG.values.find { |words| line =~ words }) || kind if line
      @verses += 1 if result && result != :unlocked
      if result == :ok
        learned(kind) if kind
        # its last verse is ability, and then it's done by itself
        result = all_known? && kind != :ability ? :complete : nil
      end
      if result
        kill_loresing
        return result
      end
      next if line

      # the reply to the last verse can land after loresing.lic has already exited
      exited_at ||= Time.now unless Script.running?('loresing')
      return :done if exited_at && Time.now - exited_at > 1.5
      if Time.now > end_time
        kill_loresing
        return :done
      end
      sleep 0.1
    end
  end

  # One verse with no keyword: :ok, :weak, :no_power, :wrong_noun, :unlocked, :end, or
  # :nothing (previously learned, or no reply)
  def self.sing_verse(item, words)
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    lines = collect("loresing #{item.noun} #{words}", VERSE_DONE, timeout: 6, settle: Regexp.union(VERSE_OK, END_OF_SONG))
    @verses += 1
    text = lines.join("\n")
    return :wrong_noun if text =~ WRONG_NOUN
    return :no_power   if text =~ NO_POWER
    return :weak       if text =~ WEAK
    return :end        if text =~ END_OF_SONG || text =~ NOTHING_NEW
    return :nothing    unless text =~ VERSE_OK

    learned(:plain)
    text =~ UNLOCKED ? :unlocked : :ok
  end

  # Carry on at the verse that failed, until all four are in or the song is at its end.
  # Returns :complete, :end, :capped, :wrong_noun, or :gone (dead, or it left the hand).
  def self.resume(item, result)
    msg "#{item.name}: verse #{[@place + 1, 4].min} failed, carrying on from there."
    # killed on its last verse, it may have got as far as "speak common"
    @guildspeak = false
    # loresing.lic may have just sung the first of the two, so start with the second
    turn = 1
    loop do
      return :capped if @verses >= max_verses
      return :gone unless ready?(item, result == :no_power)

      speak 'bard'
      result = sing_verse(item, plain_songs[turn % plain_songs.size])
      turn += 1
      case result
      when :unlocked         then return :complete
      when :end, :wrong_noun then return result
      when :ok               then return :complete if all_known? || @place == 4
      else sleep 1 # a failed verse has no roundtime
      end
    end
  end

  # mana, no song-manager (a prep script or go4invoker may have started it again), and the
  # item still in hand
  def self.ready?(item, out_of_power = false)
    quiet_songs if Script.running?('song-manager')
    rest_for_mana(out_of_power)
    !dead? && right_id == item.id.to_s
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- one item
  # returns false when the whole run should stop
  def self.sing_to(item)
    unless hold(item)
      @skipped << "#{item.name} (couldn't pick it up)"
      return true
    end

    case recall(item)
    when :unlocked
      @already << "#{item.name} (#{@owner})"
      return finish(item)
    when :not_held
      @skipped << "#{item.name} (not in your hand)"
      return finish(item)
    end

    @known  = []
    @place  = 0
    @verses = 0
    mana = checkmana
    passes = 0
    while passes < max_passes && @verses < max_verses
      passes += 1
      result = ready?(item) ? loresing_pass(item) : :gone
      result = resume(item, result) if %i[weak no_power].include?(result)
      case result
      when :no_script
        finish(item)
        return false
      when :wrong_noun
        @skipped << "#{item.name} (the song doesn't reach it as \"#{item.noun}\")"
        return finish(item)
      when :gone
        return false if dead?

        @skipped << "#{item.name} (it left your hand)"
        return true
      end

      if recall(item) == :unlocked
        msg "#{item.name}: UNLOCKED after #{count(@verses)}, mana #{mana} -> #{checkmana}."
        @unlocked << "#{item.name} (#{count(@verses)})"
        return finish(item)
      end
      msg "#{item.name}: still locked after #{count(@verses)}, mana #{mana} -> #{checkmana}."
    end

    @failed << "#{item.name} (#{count(@verses)})"
    finish(item)
  end

  def self.count(verses)
    "#{verses} #{verses == 1 ? 'verse' : 'verses'}"
  end

  def self.finish(item)
    speak 'common'
    return true if put_back

    @stop_reason = "#{item.name} wouldn't go back in the #{@container.name}; it's in your hand"
    false
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the run
  def self.main
    # Lich keeps this module and its @variables between runs
    instance_variables.each { |var| remove_instance_variable(var) }
    @already  = []
    @unlocked = []
    @failed   = []
    @skipped  = []
    @guildspeak = false

    name = Script.current.vars[0].to_s.strip
    if name.empty? || name =~ /\A-*help\z/i
      respond "[sing_all #{VERSION}] ;sing_all <container you're wearing or holding>, for example ;sing_all mantle"
      return
    end

    @container = find_container(name)
    unless @container
      msg "You aren't wearing or holding a container called \"#{name}\"."
      return
    end

    before_dying { SingAll.cleanup }
    items = look_in(@container)
    if items.empty?
      msg "Nothing in the #{@container.name}."
      return
    end
    msg "#{items.size} #{items.size == 1 ? 'item' : 'items'} in the #{@container.name}."

    quiet_songs
    msg 'Stopped playsongs: the singing needs your hands.' if stop_script('playsongs')
    stop_script('loresing')
    unless free_right_hand
      msg "Couldn't empty your right hand."
      return
    end

    items.each_with_index { |item, index|
      @current = item
      keep_going = sing_to(item)
      @current = nil
      next if keep_going

      left = items.size - index - 1
      bold "Stopping: #{@stop_reason || 'you died'}. #{left} #{left == 1 ? 'item' : 'items'} not reached."
      break
    }
    summary
  end

  def self.summary
    bold "Done with the #{@container.name}."
    {
      'Unlocked' => @unlocked, 'Already unlocked' => @already,
      'NOT unlocked' => @failed, 'Skipped' => @skipped
    }.each { |label, list| respond "    #{label}: #{list.join(', ')}" unless list.empty? }
    respond '    song-manager is still off (;song-manager starts it; Fizzlestiks-prep does too).'
  end

  # the container goes back to the right hand it came from; whatever was in the left hand
  # (brought back by fill_right_hand) goes back to the left
  def self.swap_back
    return unless @swapped && left_id == @container.id.to_s

    waitrt?
    collect('swap', SWAP_DONE, timeout: 3)
    wait_for(2) { right_id == @container.id.to_s }
  end

  # every way out, ;k included: no loresing left running, item back in the container
  def self.cleanup
    kill_loresing
    speak 'common'
    put_back if @current && right_id == @current.id.to_s
    fill_right_hand if @emptied_right && right_id.nil?
    swap_back
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "[sing_all] cleanup: #{e.message}"
  end
end

SingAll.main
